# Recruiting — main endpoints. Generated skeleton, synthetic data only.
# Path ids below are placeholders — replace with real ids from a list call.
@rejectReason = 1
@channel = 1
# Variables: see rest/http-client.env.json (host, session, xsrf). How to get them: docs/guides/api.md
# Full list of Recruiting operations: /api/docs (tag "Recruiting").

### GET /api/pipelines — recruiting.pipelines.index
GET {{host}}/api/pipelines
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}

### POST /api/pipelines — recruiting.pipelines.store
POST {{host}}/api/pipelines
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Example name",
    "stages": [
        {
            "name": "Example name",
            "kind": "attract"
        }
    ]
}

### GET /api/reject-reasons — ?all=1 → inactive too (admin screens); default → active only (reject prompt)
GET {{host}}/api/reject-reasons
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}

### POST /api/reject-reasons — recruiting.reject-reasons.store
POST {{host}}/api/reject-reasons
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Example name"
}

